<title>USA: Excel Technology Q4 profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Excel Technology Q4 profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr primary profit	 $0.12     loss	 $0.44</p>
<p> Shr diluted profit	  0.12     loss	  0.44</p>
<p> Net profit		   1,181     loss	 3,596</p>
<p> Revs			  14,272		   12,842</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	   9,749		    8,324</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted	   9,762		    8,324</p>
<p>	 (All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE - Current year primary per share and net earnings include $54,000 stock dividends. Year-ago includes reduction of $41,000 for quarter and $162,000 for year for stock divs.</p>
<p>		12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr primary pft	  $0.50     loss	 $0.21</p>
<p> Shr diluted pft	   0.50     loss	  0.21</p>
<p> Net profit		 4,893     loss	 1,596</p>
<p> Revs			57,462		   43,914</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	 9,618		    8,281</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted	 9,862		    8,281</p>
<p>	 (All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Due to 1995 loss, Excel said common stock equivalents and conversion of preferred stock was anti-dilutive and not included in the primary and fully diluted calculations for the year ago quarter and year.</p>
